<title>SOUTH AFRICA: MIH HEADLINE SHR LOSSES DEEPEN, NO DIV.</title>
<headline>MIH HEADLINE SHR LOSSES DEEPEN, NO DIV.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)	 </p>
<p>    - headline loss	 196.6	   vs     121.2</p>
<p>    - attrib		  854.1 gain    vs     27.8 loss</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   1,938 gain    vs     63 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   2,364 gain    vs     85 loss</p>
<p>    Tax			    12	   vs     5</p>
<p>    Finance costs		94	   vs     15</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,583	   vs     1,249</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     2,560	   vs     60</p>
<p>    Share of associates'	5 loss    vs     20 loss</p>
<p>Full name: MIH Holdings Ltd (Media)</p>
<p>NOTE - There was no dividend declared. The company said</p>
<p>results were not fully comparable to the previous year due to</p>
<p>changes within the group.</p>
<p>A net profit of 2.5 billion arose from the Canal Plus SA</p>
<p>European merger which was accounted for in the current</p>
<p>financial year as it was unconditional at the year end.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
